{
  "description": "Each Slayer task that has a Slayer boss, the boss, and the name of every NPC that dies in one of its kills, as the game's NPC definitions give it (SlayerBosses), so a task done on its boss can be told from one done on the task's own monsters. Also the superior Slayer monsters of the tasks with a boss or a Catacombs variant, which that decision leaves out. The list of Slayer bosses is listSource's: the bosses that each require a task for the boss itself or the equivalent monster, fought on a regular task; bosses only assigned as boss tasks, and bosses that count for a task without needing one, are not rows. Each row cites the boss's own article, which names the task. The Kraken lies as a \"Whirlpool\" until disturbed and dies as the \"Kraken\"; the whirlpool's name is left out, since cave kraken lie as whirlpools too. Each NPC keeps one id that has its name, to show where the name came from; only the names are read. Ids are RuneLite 1.13.6 gameval constants (net.runelite.api.gameval); \"constant\" names the constant each id was taken from.",
